select $q$Medical-Surgical$q$,$q$sata$q$,$q$On postoperative day 3 after total knee replacement, which findings should the nurse recognize as possible signs of deep vein thrombosis or pulmonary embolism? Select all that apply.$q$,$q$[{"id":"a","text":"New sudden chest pain with shortness of breath"},{"id":"b","text":"Warmth and redness over the affected calf"},{"id":"c","text":"Bilateral ankle stiffness in the morning"},{"id":"d","text":"Unilateral calf swelling and tenderness"},{"id":"e","text":"Incisional pain of 3/10 that improves with medication"}]$q$::jsonb,$q${"ids":["a","b","d"]}$q$::jsonb,$q$One-sided calf swelling, tenderness and warmth suggest a deep vein thrombosis, and sudden chest pain with dyspnea suggests the clot has traveled to the lungs. Expected incisional pain that responds to medication and bilateral stiffness are not typical clot signs.$q$,'draft',$q$Reduction of Risk Potential$q$,$q$Recognize Cues$q$,'pending',$q$diagnostic-parts-b-d-2026-09$q$,$q$DRAFT for clinical review. Requires an approving clinical reviewer and structured references before publication. Diagnostic B21 (Part B); intended difficulty easy; subtopic: DVT and pulmonary embolism.$q$,$q$One-sided calf swelling, tenderness and warmth suggest a deep vein thrombosis, and sudden chest pain with dyspnea suggests the clot has traveled to the lungs. Expected incisional pain that responds to medication and bilateral stiffness are not typical clot signs.$q$,$q${"a":{"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Sudden chest pain with shortness of breath may indicate a pulmonary embolism."},"b":{"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Warmth and redness of the calf are signs of deep vein thrombosis."},"c":{"is_correct":false,"explanation":"Bilateral morning stiffness suggests arthritis, not a clot."},"d":{"is_correct":true,"explanation":"One-sided calf swelling and tenderness are signs of deep vein thrombosis."},"e":{"is_correct":false,"explanation":"Mild incisional pain that responds to analgesia is expected after surgery."}}$q$::jsonb
